WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.400
Speaker 1: For those who are sick of hearing
about Donald Trump's campaign for 2020 for

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.460
his Republican nomination, today may be a
welcome change for you.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:16.240
We are going to take a deeper dive into the
last 48 hours of the Ron DeSantis candidacy

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.619
for the 2024 Republican presidential nomination.

00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:23.449
Now, one of the things that will not please
those who are sick of hearing about Trump

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:29.170
is that DeSantis is widely emulating Trump
so far in the early days of his campaign in

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:35.340
a number of different ways, including even
some of the insults that Trump became famous

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.340
for.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:41.700
So Ron DeSantis spoke in Iowa yesterday, and
there are a number of different, disturbing

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.930
and comical realities.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:49.620
First and foremost, we talked yesterday about
how Ron DeSantis said he would very much consider

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.239
pardoning Donald Trump if he were to become
president.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:58.010
If you're running against Trump, you're not
going to win by saying, I'll pardon him because

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:03.180
the people who want Trump will vote for Trump,
and the people who are disgusted by Trump

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.030
aren't going to want to go with the guy that
says, I will pardon Trump, who you want to

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.180
get away from.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.960
You're not going to beat Trump by avoiding
conflict and criticism the way that DeSantis

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.860
has done to a degree in the pre-campaign stages
of the last few months.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:26.290
And you're certainly not going to defeat Trump
by using the same insults that some people

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:27.290
like.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:32.110
In which case they'd vote for Trump and some
people don't like, in which case they're not

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.280
going to vote for the guy.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.540
Copying the insults.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.300
And Ron DeSantis yesterday during this speech
in Iowa.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:42.840
Going with the Biden is in the basement thing,
which is a Trump thing.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.850
This was Trump's line throughout the 2020
campaign.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:52.520
Speaker 2: Our great American comeback starts
by sending Joe Biden back to his basement

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:53.900
in Delaware.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.409
Speaker 1: Okay, you're not going to win this
way, Ron.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:02.280
I mean, this is if if there's a couple different
issues here.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:08.430
First, he needs to defeat Trump before he
gets a shot at Joe Biden.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:15.590
And so I you all know, I don't get into this
whole Alpha beta way of discussing everything

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:18.680
by the standards of these right wingers.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:25.060
It's not very alpha to go after the guy you're
not even running against in order to avoid

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.090
conflict with the guy who's actually up 30
points in the polls.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.800
Now, we're going to talk about polling a little
bit later because since his announcement,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.410
DeSantis is actually up 15% in the polling.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:45.990
Now, let's remember, 15% and 15 percentage
points are two different things.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:49.080
Before I get emails saying, David, what are
you talking about?

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.240
DeSantis is up 15% in the polls.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.690
We'll talk about that later.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:59.730
But this seems to be a bump and not a shift
in the underlying dynamics of this campaign,

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:04.980
which are that the majority of the Republican
Party is fine with Trump.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:10.680
And those that aren't aren't looking for a
guy with the same insults and the same hand

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.030
movements who's unwilling to actually take
Trump on head on and instead is going to go

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.030
after Joe Biden.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.030
All right.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.430
Let's look at some more clips from this speech.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:22.200
Here is DeSantis talking about the debt deal.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.540
And, you know, one of the really interesting
things about American politics, where there

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.940
is a history of state level officials vying
for national office.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:39.660
Bill Clinton was the governor of Arkansas
and then ran for president.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:47.629
What Bill Clinton had that DeSantis very much
does not have is that even though Bill Clinton

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:52.739
was this sort of folksy Southern state governor.

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:58.640
When his campaign for president launched and
he was talking about foreign policy and debt

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:05.680
and deficit, etc., he didn't seem completely
in over in over his head.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:13.040
You're going to hear Ron DeSantis talk about
debt and you will see that this state elected

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:19.829
official seems completely out of his element
and completely in over his head when discussing

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:24.370
the topics that are relevant to the national
political scene.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:32.960
Speaker 2: We now see Washington is now cooked
up their latest, quote, debt deal.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:38.759
And I can tell you this Our nation was careening
towards bankruptcy before the debt deal, and

00:04:38.759 --> 00:04:43.699
it will still be careening towards bankruptcy
after this debt deal.

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:48.770
This is greenlighting $4 trillion in new debt
in less than two years.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:53.590
It took us almost 200 years to get to 4 trillion
in debt in the first place.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:58.350
Speaker 1: Now, remember, when we're talking
about the debt ceiling and the debt limit

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:04.370
and all of this stuff, aside from the fact
that most of these elected officials don't

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:09.870
even have the most basic understanding of
macroeconomics, like put that aside for a

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:10.870
second.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.270
The debt limit relates to paying obligations
that have already been authorized.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.840
It is not actually about new spending.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:25.509
When these Republicans show up and say we're
new spending, new spending, new spending.

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:31.370
All of this spending has already been agreed
upon and it has been agreed upon by our elected

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.509
officials in the House and Senate.

00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:34.060
You might say, well, I'm a Republican.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.760
And when this stuff was agreed upon, we didn't
have the House or Senate.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:42.979
But this is the process we have and this is
all spending that has already been authorized.

00:05:42.979 --> 00:05:45.660
Now we're talking about meeting our existing
obligations.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:53.080
Speaker 2: It locks in inflated COVID level
era levels of spending, and it keeps 98% of

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:59.810
the 87,000 new IRS agents that Joe Biden instituted.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:03.669
This is not going to solve our nation's fiscal
problems.

00:06:03.669 --> 00:06:08.729
Speaker 1: So, again, now we are just quite
literally the two Trump lines.

00:06:08.729 --> 00:06:09.729
These are.

00:06:09.729 --> 00:06:14.199
Now, I know you're trying to appeal to Republicans
and some of the stuff Trump does appeals to

00:06:14.199 --> 00:06:15.199
Republicans.

00:06:15.199 --> 00:06:17.759
And so you're going have to do some of the
same stuff.

00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:25.449
But at some point, how are you going to this
is Trump's lines delivered in a really just

00:06:25.449 --> 00:06:26.479
off putting way.

00:06:26.479 --> 00:06:27.479
Right.

00:06:27.479 --> 00:06:32.180
I mean, we're just it's going to be debt and
it was bankruptcy and so it's the Trump lines

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.120
delivered in a whiny your voice in Florida.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:44.479
Speaker 2: We run budget surpluses we have
a $1.2 trillion GDP In Florida, we'd be the

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:46.870
13th largest economy in the world if we were
a separate country.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:52.250
And yet, with 1.2 trillion economy, our state
debt is only $17 billion.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.860
Speaker 1: All right.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:57.460
So the crowd not super engaged, as you can
see.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:02.400
And DeSantis offering nothing that we might
qualify as inspiring.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:09.740
Then he went completely off the rails in delusions
